    "sha": "b5eab805d383335f2bb50c85a427735b518fa997",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGI1ZWFiODA1ZDM4MzMzNWYyYmI1MGM4NWE0Mjc3MzViNTE4ZmE5OTc",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-20T20:01:39Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-20T20:01:39Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(2d): import SVG drawings as 2D sketch profiles\n\nA new SVG reader in camcraft-geometry reads paths, basic shapes, group\ntransforms, in-file use references, units and the viewBox into the same\nprimitives as the DXF reader. Chaining, nesting, the Sketch entity and the\nproject file are shared. Circular arcs stay arcs; Beziers and true\nellipses become lines within 0.005 mm. Y is flipped about the page.\n\nAn SVG with no physical size is refused until the caller states the unit\nof one drawing unit; a sized file refuses a caller unit. Malformed input,\nzero or negative sizes, degenerate arcs and over-budget files are refused\nby name.\n\nImportSvg is the undoable command (it wraps ImportDxf's apply and\ninvert), with the import_svg MCP tool and the cam.importSvg script verb.\n\nFixes #1880\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
